/*!
\page page_stssdHitCollection StSsdHitCollection — Collection Documentation

\ref StSsdHitCollection is the top-level container for all reconstructed Silicon
Strip Detector (SSD) hits in a single STAR event.  The SSD was the fourth layer
of the STAR inner tracker, providing double-sided silicon strip measurements.
Hits are organised in a three-level hierarchy: detector → ladder → wafer.

\see StSsdHitCollection
\see StSsdLadderHitCollection
\see StSsdWaferHitCollection
\see StSsdHit

---

\section ssd_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
StSsdHitCollection                 (top-level, one per event)
└── StSsdLadderHitCollection         [20 ladders, indices 0–19]
    └── StSsdWaferHitCollection        [up to 16 wafers per ladder, indices 0–15]
        └── StSPtrVecSsdHit              (owns the StSsdHit objects)
\endcode

All sub-collection nodes are embedded (stack-allocated) inside their parent;
no heap allocation is used for collection nodes.

\section ssd_containment Containment Model

| Level    | Class                       | Contents                                 |
|----------|-----------------------------|------------------------------------------|
| Detector | \ref StSsdHitCollection     | 20 \ref StSsdLadderHitCollection objects |
| Ladder   | \ref StSsdLadderHitCollection | 16 \ref StSsdWaferHitCollection objects |
| Wafer    | \ref StSsdWaferHitCollection | `StSPtrVecSsdHit` of `StSsdHit*`         |

\section ssd_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StSsdWaferHitCollection holds its hits in a member of type
\c StSPtrVecSsdHit, which is a **smart-pointer vector** that **owns** the
\ref StSsdHit objects it contains.  The \ref StSsdWaferHitCollection destructor
explicitly deletes every hit in the vector (necessary because \ref StSsdHit
provides its own pool-allocated \c new/delete).

Ladder and wafer sub-collections are embedded members of their parent classes
and are destroyed automatically with the parent.  \ref StSsdHitCollection itself
is owned by the StEvent framework (\c St_DataSet / \c StXRefMain).

\warning Do **not** delete individual \ref StSsdHit pointers obtained from the
collection.  The collection manages their lifetimes.

\section ssd_members Data Members

\subsection ssd_members_top StSsdHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StSsdLadderHitCollection[20]` | `mLadders` | Fixed-size array of 20 ladder sub-collections. |

\subsection ssd_members_ladder StSsdLadderHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StSsdWaferHitCollection[16]` | `mWafers` | Fixed-size array of up to 16 wafer sub-collections. |

\subsection ssd_members_wafer StSsdWaferHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `StSPtrVecSsdHit` | `mHits` | Smart-pointer vector of `StSsdHit*`; owns all contained hits. |

\section ssd_methods Key Methods

\subsection ssd_methods_top StSsdHitCollection

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `addHit(StSsdHit*)` | `bool` | Routes hit to correct ladder/wafer. Returns `false` if indices are out of range. |
| `numberOfHits() const` | `unsigned int` | Total hits across all ladders and wafers. |
| `numberOfLadders() const` | `unsigned int` | Always 20. |
| `ladder(unsigned int)` | `StSsdLadderHitCollection*` | 0-based ladder access; returns `nullptr` if out of range. |

\subsection ssd_methods_ladder StSsdLadderHitCollection

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `numberOfHits() const` | `unsigned int` | Total hits on this ladder. |
| `numberOfWafers() const` | `unsigned int` | Always 16. |
| `wafer(unsigned int)` | `StSsdWaferHitCollection*` | 0-based wafer access; returns `nullptr` if out of range. |

\subsection ssd_methods_wafer StSsdWaferHitCollection

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `hits()` | `StSPtrVecSsdHit&` | Mutable reference to the hit vector. |
| `hits() const` | `const StSPtrVecSsdHit&` | Const reference to the hit vector. |

\section ssd_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StSsdHitCollection* ssdColl = event->ssdHitCollection();
if (!ssdColl) return;

for (unsigned int iLad = 0; iLad < ssdColl->numberOfLadders(); ++iLad) {
    const StSsdLadderHitCollection* ladderColl = ssdColl->ladder(iLad);
    if (!ladderColl) continue;

    for (unsigned int iWaf = 0; iWaf < ladderColl->numberOfWafers(); ++iWaf) {
        const StSsdWaferHitCollection* waferColl = ladderColl->wafer(iWaf);
        if (!waferColl) continue;

        const StSPtrVecSsdHit& hits = waferColl->hits();
        for (const StSsdHit* hit : hits) {
            // process hit ...
        }
    }
}
\endcode
*/
